# ISM3232 - Module 2: zsh Navigation and File Operations

## Commands Practiced

| Command | What it does |
|--------|--------------|
| pwd | Prints the current working directory |
| ls | Lists visible files and folders |
| ls -la | Lists all files including hidden files |
| cd .. | Moves up one directory level |
| cd ~ | Returns to the home directory |
| cd ~/ism3232 | Moves to the course folder |
| tree -L 2 | Shows a directory tree up to two levels deep |
| touch notes.txt | Creates a new file |
| touch commands.txt | Creates a new file |
| touch hello_week2.py | Creates a new file |
| echo 'Week 2 navigation practice' > notes.txt | Writes text into a file |
| cat notes.txt | Displays file contents |
| head -1 notes.txt | Shows the first line of the file |
| cp notes.txt notes_backup.txt | Copies a file |
| mv hello_week2.py week2_script.py | Renames a file |
| python3 week2_script.py | Runs the Python script |
| rm notes_backup.txt | Deletes the backup file |
| code . | Opens the current folder in VS Code |
| code week2_script.py | Opens a file in VS Code |

